<title>BELGIUM: EU begins anti-dumping probe into permanganate.</title>
<headline>EU begins anti-dumping probe into permanganate.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union has begun anti-dumping inquiries into imports of potassium permanganate from India and Ukraine, the EU's Official Journal said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The (European) Commission has received a complaint... alleging that imports of potassium permanganate originating in India and Ukraine are being dumped and thereby causing material injury to the Community industry,&quot; said the Journal, dated April 26 but received on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Commission inquiries, which come after complaints by the European Chemical Industry Council, will centre on allegations of &quot;substantial&quot; dumping margins in both cases.</p>
<p>The notice said interested parties should make themselves known and give information within 40 days of the Journal's publication.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800 (PIC)</p>
</text>
